## B.3 Mode-1 zero and accepting-path sum consistency — explicit scope statement

* **Mode-1 zero can be asserted and is non-synthetic.** The six `mode1-*` scenarios run with `en=false` (`:1190-1196`), `run_scenario` forwards that to `reset(enable)` (`:1052-1053`), and `tick()` drives `top->nonblock_enable_i = 0` every cycle (`:569`). Therefore `d_nonblock_fire == 0` is an invariant of the disabled scenarios, not an expectation about hit latency — the added `CHECK` fires only if the TL performs nonblock work while the runtime enable is low. **Assumption to verify (not supplied):** that `nonblock_fire_o` is gated by `nonblock_enable_i` inside `rv_iommu_tl_wrap.sv`. If it is not gated, that check reports a real enable-honouring finding and should be escalated to Codex, never masked.
* **Enabled scenarios are not constrained** — no `mode2-*` scenario asserts `fire>0`; whether a nonblock event occurs depends on the TL policy, so this stays guard-free until the stimulus can guarantee an opportunity.
* **Accepting-path sum consistency is printed, not asserted yet.** With only `dbg_tl_req_valid/ready` plus `nonblock_fire_o` exposed, the defensible relation is `Σ d_nonblock_fire ≤ Σ n_tl_accept` inside the same window (every nonblock fire must sit under an accepted TL request). That statement additionally requires that `nonblock_fire_o` is asserted as part of a request accepted on `trans_req_*` — a property of `rv_iommu_tl_wrap.sv` that is **not in the supplied context**. Hence the two numbers are emitted side by side in `COUPLED-SUMMARY`; once the parent confirms the relation in the TL source, it can be promoted to a hard `CHECK` (and, if a candidate/probe counter is later exposed on the top, it can be added the same way — a genuine observed count, never a synthesized one).

## B.4 Assumptions / acceptance checks

* Assumption 1: `top->nonblock_fire_o` / `nonblock_busy_o` exist as outputs of the compiled `nonblock_banked_top` (verified against `nonblock_banked_top.sv:150-151`; they are already read in the current file at `:1045-1046`, so the C++ names are valid).
* Assumption 2: the counters are read after `top->eval()` in `tick()` (`:582-583`), so they are sampled at the settled clk-low point like the other TL counters.
* Assumption 3: baseline capture at `scenario_start` matches the existing `cycles=` reporting reference (`:1111`, `:1176`); `reset()` zeroes the counters anyway, so the delta equals the window count.
* Acceptance checks for a fresh run: (i) `COUPLED-SUMMARY` lines now carry `nonblock_fire=… nonblock_busy=…`; (ii) all six `mode1-*` lines show `nonblock_fire=0` and no new FAIL; (iii) no `mode2-*` line gains a hit expectation; (iv) scenario ordering, per-scenario `cycles`, byte-verification, quiet checks and the `FAILED n/m` exit code are unchanged; (v) `tests/nonblock_coupled_test.cpp` compiles with the same Verilator command used for the certified depth-512 RR run.
